      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "85c0ffbd9353bfccaea1e7175abccac3eb42674538ff0228733f7180eeb43290",
      "evidence_id": "ev-85c0ffbd9353-0000-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "APPEARANCES: ROBERT M. LOEB, Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the Petitioner."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1371",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "85c0ffbd9353bfccaea1e7175abccac3eb42674538ff0228733f7180eeb43290",
      "evidence_id": "ev-85c0ffbd9353-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. LOEB: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: In this case, the government seeks to transform a violation of a car rental agreement into a rule where unlisted drivers have no ability to even invoke the Fourth Amendment."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1371",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "85c0ffbd9353bfccaea1e7175abccac3eb42674538ff0228733f7180eeb43290",
      "evidence_id": "ev-85c0ffbd9353-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Could he have been -- could he have been the renter, given his criminal record?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1371",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "85c0ffbd9353bfccaea1e7175abccac3eb42674538ff0228733f7180eeb43290",
      "evidence_id": "ev-85c0ffbd9353-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: So that -- so that allows him to escape from those provisions?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1371",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "85c0ffbd9353bfccaea1e7175abccac3eb42674538ff0228733f7180eeb43290",
      "evidence_id": "ev-85c0ffbd9353-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 16,
        "start": 16
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. LOEB: Our rule is that if you are given permission by the renter to store items, of your personal items in the trunk, you have a reasonable expectation of privacy in it, especially when, as the government concedes, his presence in the car -"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1371",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "85c0ffbd9353bfccaea1e7175abccac3eb42674538ff0228733f7180eeb43290",
      "evidence_id": "ev-85c0ffbd9353-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: -- if I can -- if I can follow up on -- on Justice Sotomayor's question and -- and Justice Breyer's in terms of what's the clear line we can draw here."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Loeb",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1371",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "85c0ffbd9353bfccaea1e7175abccac3eb42674538ff0228733f7180eeb43290",
      "evidence_id": "ev-85c0ffbd9353-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. LOEB: Right. Unless you're committing a criminal trespass or, in the case of the car, the car thief, and especially when you were locking your personal things in the trunk -\u00ad"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1371",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "85c0ffbd9353bfccaea1e7175abccac3eb42674538ff0228733f7180eeb43290",
      "evidence_id": "ev-85c0ffbd9353-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 51,
        "start": 51
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: We have never incorporated private rights into the Fourth Amendment. We've said that we either look to property or tort law to define private rights. If the issue was what the owner versus a authorized user's rights are, we don't do that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1371",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "85c0ffbd9353bfccaea1e7175abccac3eb42674538ff0228733f7180eeb43290",
      "evidence_id": "ev-85c0ffbd9353-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 67,
        "start": 67
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Does the son of a father who owns the car but is not an authorized driver on insurance and, as a result, is not listed on the registration or the insurance card, does that son -- now we're out of the renter situation, we're in the ownership situation -- does that son have an expectation of privacy?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1371",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "85c0ffbd9353bfccaea1e7175abccac3eb42674538ff0228733f7180eeb43290",
      "evidence_id": "ev-85c0ffbd9353-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: But he's been sitting there and using it as a place where he has some privacy."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1371",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "85c0ffbd9353bfccaea1e7175abccac3eb42674538ff0228733f7180eeb43290",
      "evidence_id": "ev-85c0ffbd9353-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 71,
        "start": 71
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: What about other criminal activity? So why do you draw a line between a criminal trespasser and somebody who has an open -- an open bottle of alcohol in the car, or someone who gets in the car intoxicated or someone who is ingesting other control -"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1371",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "85c0ffbd9353bfccaea1e7175abccac3eb42674538ff0228733f7180eeb43290",
      "evidence_id": "ev-85c0ffbd9353-0003-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 72,
        "start": 72
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. LOEB: Rakas, and the Court before it in Jones, talked about wrongful presence in the car and gave the example in the Rakas footnotes of the car thief and -- and the criminal trespasser."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1371",
